  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t+{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t.$",
  "worked_solution": "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t+{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}+3{t}^{2}-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
